<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">=F0=9F=93=9D Jun=
ior Level Questions</h3>
<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1">Basic Understanding Ve=
rification</h4>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Q1: What is the main dif=
ference between Vite and Webpack?</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>=E2=9D=8C Surface Answer=
:</strong>
<em>"Vite is faster than Webpack."</em></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>=E2=9C=85 Comprehensive =
Answer:</strong>
*"The fundamental difference lies in their development philosophy and archi=
tecture:</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Webpack</strong> follows=
 a 'bundle-first' approach where it analyzes the entire dependency graph, t=
ransforms all modules, and creates bundles before serving to the browser. T=
his ensures consistency but results in slower startup times.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Vite</strong> uses a 'se=
rve-first' approach that leverages native ES modules. It pre-bundles depend=
encies using esbuild and transforms source code on-demand when requested by=
 the browser. This dramatically reduces initial startup time.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The key insight is that they sol=
ve the same problem (module bundling) but optimize for different constraint=
s - Webpack optimizes for production delivery, Vite optimizes for developme=
nt experience."*</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>=F0=9F=93=8A Follow-up Q=
uestions:</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Can you explain what ES modules=
 are and why they enable Vite's approach?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">What happens when a browser doe=
sn't support ES modules?</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Why doesn't Webpack use the sam=
e approach?</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Q2: When would you choos=
e Webpack over Vite?</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>=E2=9D=8C Incomplete Ans=
wer:</strong>
<em>"When you have a complex project."</em></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>=E2=9C=85 Strategic Answ=
er:</strong>
*"Webpack remains the better choice in several scenarios:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Legacy Browser Support<=
/strong>: If IE11 support is mandatory and you can't use polyfills</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Complex Build Pipeline<=
/strong>: Projects requiring custom loaders, complex asset processing, or b=
uild-time code generation</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Mature Ecosystem Depend=
encies</strong>: When your project relies heavily on webpack-specific plugi=
ns/loaders</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Module Federation</stro=
ng>: For micro-frontend architectures requiring runtime module sharing</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Team Expertise</strong>=
: When the team has deep Webpack knowledge and limited time for learning ne=
w tools</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The decision should be based on =
project constraints, not just performance metrics."*</p>
